@startuml BLE Concurrency

title Thread Interaction, Data Flow, and Shutdown

skinparam noteBorderColor #BBBBBB
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFF0
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #888888
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FAFAFA

box "Ride Task Thread  (producer)" #E3F2FD
    participant "RideTask" as RT
    participant "commitEnsemble()" as CE
end box

participant "BleLiveStream\n(singleton)" as BLS #EDE7F6
participant "TransportService\n(singleton)" as TS #F3E5F5

box "SpscQueue<T,N>  (lock-free ring buffer)" #E8F5E9
    participant "recordQueue_\nSpscQueue<HighRateImuRecord, 512>" as RQ
    participant "lowRateQueue_\nSpscQueue<LowRateChunk, 8>" as LQ
    participant "recorderQueue_\nSpscQueue<RecorderChunk, 8>" as RecQ
end box

box "Transport Thread  (consumer)" #FFF3E0
    participant "serviceOnce()" as SO
end box

participant "SFBLE\n(BLE wrapper)" as BLE #FAFAFA
participant "Watch / Central" as W

== High-Rate IMU Path ==

RT -> TS: enqueueImuRecord(record)
TS -> RQ: push(record)\nhead_.store(next, memory_order_release)

note over RQ
  Producer's release store on head_
  publishes the buffer write.
  Consumer's acquire load pairs
  with it - guarantees visibility.
  Each thread reads its own index
  with relaxed (sole writer).
end note

SO -> RQ: pop(record)\ntail_.load(relaxed)\nhead_.load(memory_order_acquire)
SO -> SO: appendEnsemble() - batch records into TxPacket\nfinalize() when full or remainingPayload == 0
SO -> BLE: notifyTelemetry(packet.bytes, len)
BLE -> W: GATT notification

== Low-Rate Ensemble Path  (commitEnsemble) ==

RT -> CE: commitEnsemble(pData, len)

CE -> TS: enqueueRecorderPayload(pData, len)
TS -> RecQ: push(RecorderChunk)\nhead_.store(next, release)

CE -> BLS: enqueueEnsemble(pData, len)
BLS -> TS: enqueueLowRateEnsemble(pData, len)
TS -> LQ: push(LowRateChunk)\nhead_.store(next, release)

SO -> RecQ: pop(chunk) - drain 1 per round
SO -> LQ: pop(chunk) - drain 1 per round\npacketize -> finalize() -> notifyTelemetry()
SO -> BLE: notifyTelemetry(packet)
BLE -> W: GATT notification

== Fair Scheduling  (per serviceOnce() round) ==

note over SO
  do {
    for i in [0, MAX_RECORD_BATCH=32):
      pop from recordQueue_ -> append/finalize
    pop 1 from lowRateQueue_ -> packetize
    pop 1 from recorderQueue_ -> putBytes()
    pop 1 from txQueue_ -> notifyTelemetry()
  } while (progress && (stopRequested_ || !allEmpty))

  if (hasData && millis() - lastFlushMs > 1000ms)
    -> periodic flush keeps low-rate stream alive
end note

== Shutdown / Drain Sequence ==

RT -> TS: shutdown()
TS -> TS: accepting_.store(false, release)\n[gate closed - all enqueue* will reject]
TS -> CE: lowRateFlusher_()\n[one final ensemble before drain]
CE -> BLS: enqueueEnsemble(finalData)
BLS -> TS: enqueueLowRateEnsemble(finalData)
TS -> LQ: push(finalChunk)

TS -> TS: stop()\n  stopRequested_.store(true, release)\n  running_.store(false, release)

loop spin until drained
    TS -> TS: idle_.load(acquire) == false -> yield/delay(1ms)
end

SO -> SO: serviceOnce() - stopRequested_ true\ncontinues draining all queues
SO -> SO: all queues empty + hasData -> finalize last packet
SO -> BLE: notifyTelemetry(finalPacket)
SO -> TS: idle_.store(true, release)

note right of TS
  Queues empty, builder clean,
  stopRequested_ true -> signal idle.
  stop() spin exits.
end note

TS -> RT: shutdown() returns

== Clock Sync  (BLE Callback Thread) ==

W -> BLE: write control characteristic\n{ type=TIME_SYNC_MSG, watchUnixMs:uint64, seq:uint32 }
BLE -> BLE: handleControlEvent()\natomic_thread_fence(memory_order_acquire)

note right of BLE
  Standalone fence orders all stores
  preceding the release fence in
  setControlCallback() - publishes
  controlCallback + controlContext
  as a pair. Safe only while
  registration is a one-time init.
end note

BLE -> BLS: controlRxThunk -> handleControlRx()
BLS -> BLS: handleTimeSync(watchUnixMs, seq)\n[lock timeSyncMutex_]\nrawOffsetMs = watchUnixMs - boardMillis()\nsmoothedOffsetMs = (3 * prev + rawOffsetMs) / 4\nquality -= 10 on seq gap

RT -> BLS: estimateUnixTime(boardMillis)\n[lock timeSyncMutex_]

note right of BLS
  Snapshots smoothedOffsetMs under mutex.
  Returns 0 if:
    - !valid  (no sync received yet)
    - age > 60000ms  (stale)
    - estimate <= 0
  Otherwise: (boardMillis + smoothedOffset) / 1000
end note

BLS -> RT: uint32_t unix seconds (or 0)

@enduml
